corrections.original:
In which region of a Linux process does each live?

```c
int a = 5;
static int b;
void f(void) {
  int c = 1;
  int *d = malloc(4);
}
```

(`*d` means the 4 bytes `d` points to.)

corrections.correction:
Assume an unoptimised conventional Linux C build where these objects are retained and automatic variables use stack storage. In which region does each live?

```c
int a = 5;
static int b;
void f(void) {
  int c = 1;
  int *d = malloc(4);
}
```

Assume allocation succeeds; `*d` labels the allocated four bytes.

